  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Find, **in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place**, the two solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x=\\frac{5}{4}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$ \n{{field-1}} and $x=$ \n{{field-2}}.",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x=\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(\\frac{4}{5})=0.674\\,741\u2026\u22480.674\\,7\n$$\n\nSince $0.674\\,7$ radians lies inside the given domain, our first solution, rounded to one decimal place, is ${x}_{1}=0.7.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$\nHence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +x=\\pi +0.674\\,7\u22483.8,\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place.\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=0.7$ and $x=3.8.$",
